			"notes": "Development preview for **Minecraft 1.20.1 / Forge** and **1.21.1 / NeoForge**.\n\nDownload the ZIP for your game version. It includes ShowerCore **1.2.0-preview.20261020** and the matching Hot Bath **4.1.3-preview.20261020** snapshot, including the custom-fluid name fix. Replace old copies; keep one JAR of each mod. Install the same pair on the server and every client.\n\n### Changes since the previous dev release\n\n- Customizable materials across seven bathtub styles, seven shower styles and two duck skins, with side/top texture selection and complete body coverage.\n- Shared rectangular, rounded and circular pools, configurable dimensions, rim showers, floating ducks, seats and material refunds on dismantling.\n- Corrected flowing-water resistance, pool movement, bucket compatibility and early rejection of outdated Hot Bath dependencies.\n- Preserved custom-liquid transparency and white/black colors; water also keeps its local biome tint.\n- Fixed planner window clipping, floor/rim seating, hot-fluid steam, liquid undersides and localized dynamic-fluid names in Jade.\n- Bathtub geometry, faucet targeting/flow, custom-fluid lighting and rendering fixes from the intervening development builds.\n\n### Verified and still open\n\nBoth builds pass automated build and unit checks. The final preview JAR pair is tested through **16 native GameTests and 19 actual-client cases per version**, covering pool bucket transfers, seat/save/dismount behavior, fluid names, language changes, and liquid appearance in the world, ordinary bathtubs and pools. Earlier focused fixes have English evidence videos linked in [#40](https://github.com/CrabMods/ShowerCore/issues/40).\n\nLiquid appearance: [English before/after report](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CrabMods/ShowerCore/6cbdf22baea9f2551ffff91a45ad871501f07d18/validation/issue-53/fluid-appearance-report-en.mp4) in [#53](https://github.com/CrabMods/ShowerCore/issues/53).\n\nStill requesting reproduction details for [#30](https://github.com/CrabMods/ShowerCore/issues/30) (placement height when standing above the ground) and [#31](https://github.com/CrabMods/ShowerCore/issues/31) (liquid filling after the required Hot Bath upgrade). These remain open; they are not declared fixed by this preview.\n\nThis is a development snapshot. Back up a world before testing. Third-party player animation packs and every modpack combination are outside the current evidence. Matching custom bath datapacks are optional and are not bundled.\n\n### Source snapshots\n\n- ShowerCore: [NeoForge](https://github.com/CrabMods/ShowerCore/commit/9c3a0dc6266deb7f63fd2d9d9ba2eb328abc7c34), [Forge](https://github.com/CrabMods/ShowerCore/commit/3f1e58ba3d846052198e97f843737df05c0e101f).\n- Hot Bath: [NeoForge](https://github.com/CrabMods/hotBath/commit/41a781a62cbd45e3c905af8888ae4d4d6403a42e), [Forge](https://github.com/CrabMods/hotBath/commit/91c75c99caf6e0ca5d14d3fdc85282145cdd9970).\n\nVersion suffixes identify this preview; the release does not change stable update manifests. Individual JARs and SHA-256 checksums are also available below."
